WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.710
This film shows how to join the Downtown
safety network, and how to take part.

2
00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.860
The safety dashboard connects Downtown

3
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.180
businesses and Downtown
public-safety officers.

4
00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.247
A business registers with only an email.

5
00:00:15.297 --> 00:00:19.180
An officer joins when an
administrator sends an invitation.

6
00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:23.220
A business association can get
an access code for its members.

7
00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:26.020
Everyone can see the public live map.

8
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.390
No account is necessary.

9
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:33.820
To register a business,
open 901safety.com.

10
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.540
Select Register your business.

11
00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.620
Type your work email.

12
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.740
Then select Email me a sign-in link.

13
00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.100
Your email makes your account.

14
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.590
You do not need a password.

15
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.400
Open the email, and select Sign in.

16
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:55.170
The link works one time, and
it expires after one hour.

17
00:00:55.750 --> 00:01:01.460
If you have an access code,
open 901safety.com/join.

18
00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:06.580
The code comes from the Downtown safety
team, or from your business association.

19
00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.060
Type the code and your work email.

20
00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.060
Then select Join.

21
00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:14.150
Open the email, and finish joining.

22
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:18.300
The first time you sign in,
set up your storefront.

23
00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.380
Select Set up now.

24
00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.180
Type the business name
and the street address.

25
00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:26.033
The address puts your business on the map.

26
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:30.140
It also sets which alerts you
get, in a half-mile radius.

27
00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.700
Then select Register storefront.

28
00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.700
To sign in faster next
time, select Add passkey.

29
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.550
Then use Face ID, Touch
ID or your device PIN.

30
00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:47.220
Your home page shows the active alerts
in a half-mile radius of your business.

31
00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:50.873
Your block shows the
last 48 hours on a map.

32
00:01:50.923 --> 00:01:55.700
To report what you see, select
Talk, Form or Quick alert.

33
00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:59.780
My reports shows the status
of each report that you send.

34
00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:04.100
To hear new alerts, select
Turn on, in Spoken alerts.

35
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.990
Keep the dashboard open in a
browser tab to get alerts.

36
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:14.240
The Lookout board shows people and vehicles
that officers ask you to watch for.

37
00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:18.627
Warning: do not approach,
follow or stop anyone.

38
00:02:18.677 --> 00:02:22.120
If you see a match, select I've seen this.

39
00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:24.920
Show where you saw them, and add a note.

40
00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.720
Then select Send to officers.

41
00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.890
Officers get your sighting at once.

42
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:37.100
Neighbors, property managers and
associations can follow the public live map.

43
00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.260
No account is necessary.

44
00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:44.700
The map shows the type of each report,
its status and an approximate place.

45
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.620
It never shows names, photos or addresses.

46
00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:54.190
A business association can ask the safety
team for an access code for its members.

47
00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:58.120
Join the people who
watch out for Downtown.

48
00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.330
Scan the code to join.
